  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Synthetic Claims Triage",
    "description": "Single-tenant synthetic claims assistant. All recommendations require a human decision.\n\n## End-to-end showcase\n1. Authorize with the server's bearer token.\n2. POST /sessions and copy session_id.\n3. POST /sessions/{session_id}/batches using the starter example; copy the returned id as batch_id.\n4. POST /sessions/{session_id}/chat with the explanation, then follow-up example.\n5. Review rows 0/1/2/3 as investigate/approve/investigate/request_documentation.\n6. GET the batch again: state becomes REVIEWED after all four decisions.\n\n## Agent functions\n- **supervisor**: `route_request` \u2014 Route the exact current user request through the deterministic supervisor.\n- **intake**: `validate_claim` \u2014 Validate the bound synthetic claim row for missing fields, dates, policy identifiers and duplicates.\n- **coverage**: `check_coverage` \u2014 Retrieve underwriting rules and check the bound claim against policy coverage and earlier history.; `search_knowledge` \u2014 Retrieve cited synthetic underwriting rules from the local file vector index.\n- **briefing**: `build_brief` \u2014 Build an evidence-grounded adjuster brief and a constrained next action for the bound claim row.\n\nThese are internal, context-bound tools invoked by the workflow. Coverage retrieves rules inside check_coverage; search_knowledge is an additional registered tool. Mock mode executes local tools and persistence; it does not prove Azure inference or hosted file search. Use a new session for each independent batch demo to avoid duplicate flags.",
    "version": "1.0.0"
  },
